  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Saturday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: \n\nLarge upper level trough will continue to send rounds of showers \nand a few thunderstorms through Halloween, before the main system \nmoves overhead Sunday. Shower and storm chances will vary during \nthe day, Saturday but will run from 35% to 75%. Sunday, chances \nincrease to near 100% through Monday morning as the core of upper \nlow moves over Nevada. Snow levels Saturday will stay around 9000 \nfeet, however with the low center overhead Sunday into Monday \nmorning snow level will fall to around 6500 feet, this will allow \nfor a brief changeover for some of the higher passes like Austin, \nPinto, Sacramento, as well as for NV 225 from Wildhorse to Owyhee.\nNow for the Rubies this will bring a Winter Storm Watch in effect\nSaturday evening through early Monday morning. Precipitation \namounts have continued to trend steady, even excluding \naccumulations we have seen over the last few days, with passes and\nvalleys seeing rain yet to fall amounts of 0.10\u201d for the Black \nRock desert to 0.50\u201d for Elko, Ely, and mid-elevation passes. \nWhile higher elevation passes and mountain ranges seeing between \nup to 0.50\u201d to 1.50\u201d+ of water or water equivalent (for snowfall).\nSnowfall as temperatures cool Sunday, with a trace to 0.5\u201d \npossible for the higher elevation passes passes, and up to 1+ foot\nof snow for the range peaks above 8000 feet. Monday afternoon, as\nthe upper trough departs, high pressure will build in as the \ntrough departs bringing quieter weather back into the region this \nridge will be in place at least through Tuesday. Now for \nWednesday, Thursday and Friday of next week, models tonight have a\nmajor change up since yesterday, in keeping a active pattern over\nthe great basin. As both the GFS and ECMWF are in relative \nagreement with a pair of weaker upper level trough passing through\nWednesday and again Friday bringing chances for valley rain and \nmountain snow showers. Temperature wise for the holiday weekend \nand into next week thanks to the active pattern will be relatively\nconsistent over the weekend and into next week as highs will be \nnear to, to slightly below normal ranging in the mid 40s to upper \n50s, with lows in the mid 20s to upper 30s. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \nThere is high confidence for scattered showers and thunderstorms \ncontinuing on and off through Monday morning.\n\nThere is high confidence in the return of upper ridging Monday \nafternoon through at least Tuesday of next week which will bring a\nquick calm for the region. \n\nThere is low confidence for the upper level pattern after \nWednesday of next week, as models have changed on possible \nsolutions, now showing the active pattern continuing for the end \nof next week. &&",
